---
import Catalog from '../layouts/Catalog.astro';
---
<Catalog title="Crumza Pro" description="The full collection, wherever you build. In development.">
  <div class="note-page">
    <section><h2>Design is the starting point.</h2><p>We're building a website creator that starts with considered components instead of inventing every screen from scratch. First: fast, search-friendly Astro websites and landing pages.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Open by default.</h2><p>The UI foundations and a useful selection of blocks belong in the open-source library. Solid, frosted and liquid are part of the same system, not paid skins.</p><a href="/ui">Explore the UI library</a></section>
    <section><h2>A subscription for the full collection.</h2><p>Premium components, blocks, themes and complete business templates. The plan is to make your licensed collection available in compatible AI tools through an authenticated connection.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Carefully built, not artificially abundant.</h2><p>A small, coherent library comes first. Search will match layout, material, framework and license before choosing a component. No invented component counts, live checkout or AI generation in this preview.</p><a href="/docs/getting-started">Start with the open-source foundations</a></section>
  </div>
</Catalog>
